videos.script:
Lesson 2 gave the planner two native projects. Today you open them. {{tree}}

Most days you never will. You change the web code, build, sync, and the projects follow. But a few changes only happen on the native side. {{list}} A permission. An icon. A signature. A version number. You need to know which file each one lives in.

On Android, that means one file that describes the app, the manifest, and one line of Java. {{manifest}} On iOS, a list of keys and a Swift file. {{plist}}

Then the tools. {{studio}} Android Studio and its SDK, and an emulator or a phone. And Xcode, on a Mac. Neither could be installed where this course was recorded, so you will see what Capacitor says without them, and the steps to take with them.

And one test you can run anywhere. {{sync}} Change two files, sync, and see which change survives.
